    t=para(t,'The application compares partial railway fare',r'The application compares partial fare and frequency authority in three Chinese corridors. Commercial joint control raises profit while lowering railway-centered welfare at the central calibration. A tighter fare cap reduces the loss, whereas strict vulnerable-participation protection delivers positive welfare while retaining part of the profit gain. Income composition and conventional additions have effects conditional on pricing authority, schedule value and resources. Calibration, schedule and fleet tests establish the scope of these findings.')
    t=para(t,'The search alternates fare and integer-frequency blocks',r'The search alternates fare and frequency blocks, followed by simultaneous fare--frequency moves and independent trajectories from reference, boundary, nested-policy and counterpart starts. Independent scalar calculations verify demand and accounting. Block-local search cannot guarantee improvements requiring coordinated changes across instruments, motivating exact single-OD certification. Every HN/WC common-pricing domain is evaluated by exhaustive period enumeration and a fleet-coupled integer master. If the finance/retention-relaxed upper bound is unattainable, the master imposes additive daily profit and L-participation constraints directly and retains nondominated period columns in profit, welfare and L trips. A certificate requires an optimal master solution satisfying all original constraints and matching its upper bound within 0.01 CNY/day. Proven infeasibility and unresolved limits are recorded separately. JX and differentiated pricing retain multi-start feasible-witness and independently audited joint-neighborhood evidence.')
    t=t.replace('A certificate requires an optimal master solution','Equivalent pooled K splits use least-cost representations, and fleet constraints use exact integer-count bounds. LP reduced costs remove only columns proved unable to improve an existing feasible design. A certificate requires an optimal master solution')
    t=t.replace('JX and differentiated pricing retain multi-start feasible-witness and independently audited joint-neighborhood evidence.','Discovered JX designs are projected into the reference authority and fare menu, then reevaluated under reference demand and constraints. Improved reference designs are propagated back to the sensitivity states until this cross-scenario check is stable. JX and differentiated pricing retain multi-start feasible-witness and independently audited joint-neighborhood evidence.')
    t=t.replace('Exact certificates apply only to the stated HN/WC central reference problems.','Certificate statuses are reported for each enumerated HN/WC problem; JX and differentiated pricing use independent multi-start and joint-neighborhood checks.')
    stress=[r for g in groups('E7') if g['job']['case']=='JX' for r in g['records'] if r['feasible']]
