    v=json.loads((ROOT/'verification.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));a=json.loads((ROOT/'local_audit.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));t=para(t,r'Table~\ref{tab:experiment_overview} reports signed',r'Table~\ref{tab:experiment_overview} reports signed finer/coarser-menu and extra-round checks. Nested cap/fleet domains share feasible seeds. Independent scalar checks reproduce '+f(v['records'],0)+' main-experiment records; the independent audit evaluates '+f(a['checked_candidates'],0)+' candidates including simultaneous fare--frequency moves, with no remaining improving feasible block. Across distinct HN/WC state--policy--objective problems, '+f(R['certificate_count'],0)+' optima and '+f(R['infeasibility_count'],0)+' infeasible problems have finite-menu certificates; '+str(len(R['unresolved_certification']))+r' remain without a certificate. JX and differentiated pricing retain the search scope stated above.')
    t=t.replace('Fare authority and behavioral calibration materially change commercial gains. Upper profiles cross elasticity anchors with fare caps; lower tornados rank separately tested assumptions by the range of P3 profit gains per observed departure.','Commercial welfare remains negative on the sampled elasticity--cap grid. Upper profiles show certified HN/WC commercial optima and jointly polished JX witnesses; lower tornados use re-solved designs to rank separately tested assumptions by profit-gain ranges per observed departure.')
